.TH turequirement n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::turequirement
.PP
Parses a Mermaid \fBrequirementDiagram\fR block into a \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR model so it renders natively (SVG or PNG) through the pure\-Tcl engine. One of the graph\-type parsers the \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR facade dispatches to; normally call \fBtuflow::toPng\fR / \fBtuflow::toSvg\fR.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::turequirement 0.1
.CE
.SS Commands
.CS
::tclutils::turequirement::parse text      ;# -> tudiagram model dict
.CE
.SS "Supported syntax (Mermaid subset)"
.CS
requirement <name> { id: .. text: .. risk: .. verifymethod: .. }  -> box
element <name> { type: .. docref: .. }                            -> box
<src> - <relation> -> <dst>    (satisfies/derives/traces/...)     -> edge
<dst> <- <relation> - <src>                                       -> edge
.CE
.PP
A requirement / element box carries a \fB<<type>>\fR stereotype line, the name and the collected fields (ASCII only — the bitmap font has no guillemets).
.SS Usage
.CS
package require tclutils::turequirement
package require tclutils::tudiagram

set src {requirementDiagram
    requirement test_req {
        id: 1
        text: the system shall boot
        risk: high
        verifymethod: test
    }
    element test_entity {
        type: simulation
    }
    test_entity - satisfies -> test_req
}
::tclutils::tudiagram::writeSvg [::tclutils::turequirement::parse $src] req.svg
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
v1 limitations (honest): long field values (e.g. \fBtext:\fR) make wide boxes (no wrapping); requirement sub\-types all render as plain boxes.
.IP \(bu
Companion: \fBtclutils::tudiagram\fR (renderer), \fBtclutils::tuflow\fR (dispatch).
.SS "Error codes"
.PP
\fB\-errorcode {TCLUTILS TUREQUIREMENT <REASON>}\fR — \fBEMPTY\fR (no requirements/elements found).
